From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ruskin Constant <ruskin@cloudflare.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 17:52:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fetch each @font-face once, and only for text it covers

A <style> whose text is rewritten per rule (the CSSOM insertRule mirror,
JSS) re-registers its sheet on every mutation, and every registration
re-collected the sheet's @font-face rules: N pending copies, N fetches +
decompressions, N UNLOADED entries of which only one cleared (so the
family stayed blocked for its style). On a styled-components page that
is hundreds of copies. queue_font_faces dedupes on the full descriptor
(family, url, weight, style), matching Chrome's once-per-document font
cache. Both entry points (add_stylesheet_for_node and @import'ed sheets
via DocumentEvent::PendingFontFaces) go through it.

The lazy loader fetched a declared face once its family appeared in some
computed style. Google Fonts and next/font split every family into 5-7
script subsets, each an @font-face with a unicode-range, so a used
family pulled every subset of every weight/style it declared: a
Portuguese page loaded 26 files where Chrome loads 6.

Chrome fetches a subset only when font matching needs a glyph from it.
This lands that at document granularity: PendingFontFace carries the
descriptor's ranges, and flush_needed_font_faces also requires that some
text node contains a codepoint inside them, tested against a 136 KiB
bitset over U+0000..=U+10FFFF. The bitset is built by one O(text) scan
the first time a range-gated face needs checking; after that every text
write (create_text_node, set_node_text, append_text_to_node,
pseudo-element content) folds its codepoints in, so the style-resolve
path never walks text again. The set is monotonic, so incremental upkeep
is exact. Before the build, writes skip it: pages with no range-gated
face pay nothing. A face whose ranges cover no text stays queued and is
re-probed each flush (a few bitset words per range), so a later
script-inserted string in a new script pulls its subset then. Faces
without the descriptor behave as before.

Faces are now marked UNLOADED at fetch time rather than at declaration:
a face this gate never releases must not block its family's style in
face_pending_for_style forever. Before the first flush nothing is
delivered, so there is no mid-load substitution to guard against.

The embedder picks fallback faces for scripts it finds in the navigate
HTML. Text a script writes later never reached that scan, so it rendered
as tofu (example.com inserts Arabic and Chinese from s.js).

note_text_codepoints now counts writes that hold a codepoint past
Cyrillic, and text_uses_codepoints answers whether the document's text
touches a set of ranges, building the existing codepoint bitset on first
use. The embedder polls the counter and probes only when it moves.

Co-authored-by: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
